WEBVTT

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:07.400
Benten is neither tengu nor 
tanuki; she's just human.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:14.170
Strolling along the shore of 
Lake Biwako for no real reason,

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:21.660
young Benten had the human name Suzuki Satomi
 befitting the cute country girl which she was.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:29.090
Prof. Akadama, who happened to be at 
Lake Biwako on a New Year's visit,

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.050
took the girl home with him.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:38.140
He took great care in giving 
her a tengu education

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.090
and she enthusiastically raced up 
the ladder from human to tengu.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.400
Once she reached the top,

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:53.900
she kicked her kidnapper-turned-master to 
the curb in one flash of her gorgeous legs.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.320
Oh, Professor.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.220
You came after us, huh.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.920
The current Benten is not who she used to be.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.010
<b>Episode Six: 
Taking in Fall Colors</b>

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:50.870
Benten, you sure are active.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.840
You're pretty nimble yourself, for your age.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.610
Just a little further.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:01.340
Sheesh, you're just like a tengu.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:00.570
I'm just a Suzuki Satomi.

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.290
She's not who she used to be.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:11.830
So,

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.330
I was thinking about the day I first met you.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:19.120
How awful. Feel free to forget it.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.100
I would never! It was the 
day of the year-end bash.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.690
I heard the tanuki cage 
was in the inner parlor,

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.680
so I went to check on it.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:38.850
And you were lying next to 
it, peacefully sleeping.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.160
You had piled up some floor 
cushions to make a pillow

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:44.450
and were curled up like a child.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:46.300
Was I really?

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:49.280
I thought, "Who could that be?"

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:55.210
I didn't know the new Friday 
Fellow was a young lady.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:01.680
The tanuki in the cage was a 
splendid one, and so dignified.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.970
He didn't have the slightest hint of fear.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.840
So, the tanuki and I were 
staring at each other

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:12.420
when you woke up, came over to me,

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:15.100
and started talking to him.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.980
Are you Hotei?

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:20.410
I'll be meeting you officially this evening.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:22.660
Oh, I see!

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:27.400
You're the person Jurojin was talking 
about! I didn't know it would be a girl.

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.490
I'm Benten.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:33.440
He seems to be having a good sleep.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.610
You poor thing, you'll be eaten by me.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:42.290
But you know, I'm going to eat you up.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.680
That stuff happened so long ago I forgot.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.190
I fell for you then.

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:55.560
I fell in love.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:59.250
I could understand how you felt.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.470
I thought, "Now here's a 
girl after my own heart!" {TB: I wouldn't always translate doushi like this, but here I think it's pretty great.}

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:05.100
That's your misunderstanding.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.720
I don't remember saying anything like that.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:13.190
Hmm, but I remember...

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.260
Benten?

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:42.840
What are you doing?

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:46.770
Stay back! Stay back or I'll eat you.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:48.420
I'm serious.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:51.610
I don't mean to presume, but 
is something the matter?

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:57.030
The moon is pretty, so anyways, I got sad.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:08:01.040
I want to take a bath. I'm going home.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.080
That's so self-centered.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.570
You're just gonna leave us on the roof?

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:09.550
Yasaburo, please make sure 
the professor gets home okay.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:34.740
Where did Benten go?

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.040
I'm hungry, are you?

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:48.880
Um...

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:52.700
Have some with me.

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:02.900
I'm good at making rice balls.

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:04.160
Tasty, right?

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.630
You know, I like rice balls.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:14.170
They're good cold, they're good grilled,

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:16.810
and you can eat them anytime, anywhere.

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:24.370
We call it "Benten's Early Exit."

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:30.430
She alway disappears without 
warning part-way through.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:34.830
Yeah, can't make head or tail of her.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:47.000
You must be a student? How do you know her?

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.810
We followed the same master.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.210
Master? Master of what?

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.620
Ah, the entertainment from 
the dinner party earlier?

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:56.660
Something like that.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:59.580
So Benten can perform as well?

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:02.580
Yeah, I'm nowhere near close to her level.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:06.550
She's even surpassed our master — there's 
no one in Kyoto who can match her.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:12.380
At any rate, she sure is an eccentric beauty.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:15.740
Professor, you're a bit 
of an odd one, yourself.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:18.130
I'm not so odd.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:21.460
Your passion for eating is no joke.

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:23.800
I suppose I do have a passion for eating.

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:28.510
And I've eaten so many 
things, partly for research.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:32.000
You eat tanuki, too.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.580
Not only tanuki! I travel here 
and there throughout the world

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:40.050
eating everything, be it 
bug, plant, beast, or fish.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:41.660
Are they tasty?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:45.790
If you're going to eat something, you have to 
make it tasty. That's the duty of one who eats.

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.500
But you know, to tell the truth,

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:53.830
eating a life should be delicious on 
its own. That's the way it's gotta be.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:58.380
That's the state of mind I'm aiming 
for; that's why I eat so many things.

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:03.830
Well, but not poisonous stuff, right. 
'Cause you die.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:08.640
Me, though, I'm a small fry.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:11.440
Open your eyes to the world,

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:14.700
and you'll find humans 
eat any and everything.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:17.650
It's shocking how much of a 
passion for eating we have.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:21.650
Whenever I think of it, I'm 
filled with admiration.

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:25.640
To eat is to love.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.760
We eat so many things!

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:32.420
And we love so many things!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:33.920
Humans, banzai!

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.730
...is how you start to feel.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:41.170
But from the point of view of the 
eaten, there's no "banzai" about it.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:44.880
Of course, the eaten must hate it.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:49.700
I would hate it, too, if I got chomped 
head-first by a bear or a wolf.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.190
Anybody would hate that.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:54.410
But if I'm gonna get eaten, I want to eat.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:59.410
I feel bad for them, but I like tanuki 
so much I want to eat them up.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:07.500
This isn't limited to tanuki. 
I will eat all the cutie-patooties.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:10.310
It's a pity, but so scrumptious.

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:13.250
A fine contradiction, wouldn't you say?

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.820
That is to say, love!

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.120
I'm not entirely sure, 
but, probably love, right?

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:19.970
Must be love.

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:24.680
Humans can be easy-going like that because 
they don't have to worry about being eaten.

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:28.680
You're solidly on the side of the eaten, huh.

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:31.920
But that's a good point.

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:37.140
Certainly, humans like us don't 
have to worry about being eaten.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:38.820
No natural enemies.

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:41.690
We die, get burned, turn to ashes,

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:45.450
get eaten by microbes, and return 
to the dust — that's about it.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:50.290
But when it comes to that, 
I get this lonely feeling.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:54.330
It's sad to be abruptly eaten by microbes.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.430
If I'm gonna die anyways,

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.060
well, if it doesn't hurt too much,

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:02.570
I'd rather be eaten by a tanuki.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:09.750
I'd rather be a tanuki's dinner 
than die all wrinkly in a hospital.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:13.840
Dying in a hospital doesn't nourish anyone.

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:16.520
That's so lonely.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.820
If a tanuki got full on 
me, that'd be way better.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:26.240
Eating you would be a bit much for a tanuki.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:27.810
Hmm.

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:31.450
Besides that, I have this 
feeling I must taste horrible.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:33.910
What a pity.

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:37.590
If a tanuki ate me, he'd 
probably think I taste bad.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:41.060
It's so sad for people to feel that way.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:45.460
I've never heard of any human getting 
sad about something like that.

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:50.090
There was a tanuki saying that sort 
of thing to me back then, too.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:52.770
I can remember it even now.

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:04.480
It was the night Benten first 
joined the Friday Fellows.

00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:13.260
You're really something, huh.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:17.710
You must have made a name for 
yourself in tanuki society.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:22.070
This evening we'll be eating you.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:24.640
You're probably reluctant,

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:28.370
but we always have tanuki hot 
pot at the year-end bash.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:34.680
Being born as a tanuki means there may 
come a time you'll be eaten by humans.

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:38.760
It's selfish of me, but you know,

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:42.580
I'm happy I get to eat you.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:46.400
There's meaning in the fact that we met.

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.970
How can you be so calm?

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:52.780
You're not anxious?

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:57.520
I've done everything I wanted to do.

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:59.810
My children are grown.

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:04.160
The youngest is still small, 
but he has his brothers,

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:07.550
so I suppose all that remains is for them to 
help each other out and live a decent life.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:11.160
I sowed my seeds and 
nurtured them to an extent.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:15.550
I fulfilled my role as a tanuki.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:20.840
The rest of my days are a blessing, 
in other words, a lucky break.

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:27.480
Therefore, at this point, I don't 
mind being eaten by you at all.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.620
If you want to eat me, you should.

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.690
This is kind of weird.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:35.780
I have this feeling you're talking, 
but it must be my imagination.

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:38.270
I'm actually talking.

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:43.760
Well I'll be! You shouldn't 
surprise people like that.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:48.300
I just thought it wouldn't matter 
if I said something to you.

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:52.500
Perhaps it's the last trick of my life,

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.800
a manifestation of my idiot blood.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:01.170
And then we talked for a bit,

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:05.480
about where we were living, what kinds 
of things we ate, that kind of stuff.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.130
But there was one thing.

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:12.110
The tanuki was worried he might taste bad.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:15.170
It'll be okay.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:19.390
I'll take responsibility and make 
a delicious hot pot out of you.

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:22.320
Please see it through from beginning to end.

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:26.500
I would feel horrible if I ruined 
an otherwise tasty hot pot.

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:30.240
You're a magnificent tanuki, 
so you'll taste great.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:32.110
Don't worry.

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:36.220
As a souvenir to the afterlife, 
I'd like to ask your name.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.420
I'm Yodogawa Chotaro.

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:43.610
As I thought, you're him...

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:46.670
Hmm? You know me?

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:49.460
You helped out one of my family members.

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:52.630
In return, tell me your name as well.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:57.170
I'm Nise-emon, Shimogamo Soichiro.

00:16:57.560 --> 00:16:58.580
Who's there?

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:02.080
Hmm?

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:09.520
But... what?

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:15.420
You probably don't believe a 
story as strange as that, huh.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.890
I think I can.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:23.430
Ah, I'm glad! I told you because 
of the connection between us.

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.710
Uh, we just met for the first time tonight.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:28.290
But there's something of destiny about you.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:31.400
I feel like I've known you forever.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:34.460
Let's drink to this evening's 
encounter! A toast!

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:37.040
Is it okay for someone who is 
supposedly a college professor

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:40.660
to be drinking in a place like 
this in the middle of the night?

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.610
Nevermind, nevermind!

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:45.660
It's a manifestation of my idiot blood!

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:56.670
Hey you!

00:17:56.670 --> 00:18:00.610
What do you know? A ladder! 
We can get down this way.

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:06.990
Phew, how lucky.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:19.400
Kaisei, is that you?

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:23.660
Go home and get some sleep, lunkhead.

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:26.250
Next time you're on your own.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:30.040
Hey, Teramachi Street is this way, right?

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:31.700
Thanks.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:43.180
Big Brother, it's me.

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:45.410
Oh geez, Yasaburo!

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:48.780
So you're still alive, then. I was worried.

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:50.190
Hard to believe, but yeah, still alive.

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:55.720
You gonna abandon the world 
and become a frog, too?

00:18:56.030 --> 00:19:00.030
If two of her kids became 
frogs, Mother would cry...

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:02.450
I'm just gonna crash for the night.

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:07.300
That's fine. I thought maybe you 
were worried about something.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:13.010
You've had trouble talking about those 
things ever since you were little.

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:14.890
Worries? I have absolutely none.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:18.050
Because I decided to live an 
interesting, amusing life.

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:20.770
Why'd you come?

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:21.950
Mm.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:28.140
Come visit me at my office sometime.

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:31.810
<b>Kyoto University Yodogawa Chotaro</b>

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:35.560
Well then, see you again.

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:40.410
He said it was a "manifestation" 
of his "idiot blood."

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:45.790
This university professor Yodogawa 
says the same thing as Father!

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:50.180
Even if we owe him for saving Mother,

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:52.500
he's an enemy we should hate.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.610
But for some reason I think 
of him affectionately.

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:57.750
It's a weird thing to say, but...

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:00.520
I'm utterly bizarre.

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:04.040
Why don't I hate him?

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:07.820
I actually really like him.

00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:12.080
And why do I have to have a crush on Benten,

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:15.230
who boiled Father in a hot pot and ate him?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:20.120
It's a manifestation of our idiot blood.

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:23.350
Besides, we're tanuki.

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:26.400
Now and then we get eaten.

00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:30.370
It's not wrong for a human to eat a tanuki.

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:34.620
I admire you, Big Brother. 
You're enlightened.

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:36.130
Not at all.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:40.680
In reality, I just pretend to understand.

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:43.510
At any rate, I'm a frog in a well.

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:45.910
That's always a convenient out.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:50.060
No... I still have a lot to learn.

00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:57.560
Even now, I tear up when I think of Father.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.640
Someone's here to consult 
you about their troubles?

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:12.720
No, that's Benten.

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:13.450
What?

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:16.960
She doesn't say anything.

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:20.190
She just sits there like 
that, crying all alone.

00:21:20.890 --> 00:21:23.090
The well water is gonna get all salty.

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:25.890
I wonder why she cries.

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:28.340
I wonder what she's sad about.

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:31.450
Could it be because the moon's so pretty?

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:35.390
A child is someone who cries for no reason.

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:39.480
At that time, in Kyoto

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:45.110
my big brother Yaichiro and 
my uncle Ebisugawa Soun

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:49.240
were starting up the unsightly battle 
over who would be the next Nise-emon.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.880
But as for me,

00:21:53.510 --> 00:21:55.880
I was pretty much a frog in a well

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.500
knowing nothing of the sea.

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:34.720
Argh, none of these 
schmucks have any manners!

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:37.140
Like that! Don't wear a towel in the bathtub!

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Bathhouse Rules</b>
